e. conduct cross-institutional coordination among government institutions as well as with the community and the Business Sector;
f. conduct data collection and inventory of women's data;
g. provide safe houses.
(2) Regional Government has the authority to:
a. prepare standard operational guidelines for minimum service standards for efforts to fulfill rights and protection for women;
b. implement services for the fulfillment of rights and protection of women;
c. conduct supervision of efforts to fulfill women's rights and protection services for women; and
d. develop cooperation networks among government institutions as well as with Universities, the community and the Business Sector.

